+We work with names. For a set $X$ of coinitial $\dist$-steps write
+$\names(X) = \set{\name(\redexthree) : \redexthree \in X}$.
+A complete development of $X$ contracts each name of $X$ exactly once,
+so its names are $\names(X)$.
+Hence, by \rlem{simulation_residual_of_a_development},
+$\names(\redseqthree/\tm') = \names(\redexset/\tm')$
+whenever $\redseqthree$ is a complete development of a set $\redexset$ of coinitial $\beta$-steps.
+
+By \rcoro{permutation_equivalence_in_terms_of_names} and \rlem{names_after_projection_along_a_step},
+it suffices to prove:
+\[
+  \names((\redseq/\redseqtwo)/(\tm'/\redseqtwo)) = \names(\redseq/\tm') \setminus \names(\redseqtwo/\tm')
+  \tag{$\ast$} \label{eq:cubelemma_names}
+\]
+We prove three claims in order. The second one generalizes over \emph{sets} of steps:
+projecting a derivation $\redseq = \redex\redseq'$ over a development $\redseqthree$ leaves
+$\redseq'$ to be projected over $\redseqthree/\redex$, which is a development of a set of residuals
+even when $\redseqthree$ is a single step.
+So an induction stated only for single steps does not close.
+
+\medskip
+\noindent{\bf Claim 1 (a step after a derivation).}
+For every step $\redex$ and every derivation $\redseqthree$ coinitial with it:
+\[
+  \names((\redex/\redseqthree)/(\tm'/\redseqthree)) = \names(\redex/\tm') \setminus \names(\redseqthree/\tm')
+\]
+where $\redex/\redseqthree$ is the set of residuals of $\redex$,
+and $(\redex/\redseqthree)/(\tm'/\redseqthree) = \bigcup_{\redex' \in \redex/\redseqthree} \redex'/(\tm'/\redseqthree)$.
+By induction on $\redseqthree$. The empty case is immediate.
+If $\redseqthree = \redextwo\redseqthree'$, then
+$\redex/\redseqthree = \bigcup_{\redex'' \in \redex/\redextwo} \redex''/\redseqthree'$
+and $\tm'/\redseqthree = (\tm'/\redextwo)/\redseqthree'$, so by \ih{} (on $\tm'/\redextwo$ and each $\redex''$):
+\[
+  \begin{array}{rcll}
+  \names((\redex/\redseqthree)/(\tm'/\redseqthree))
+    & = & \bigcup_{\redex'' \in \redex/\redextwo} \names(\redex''/(\tm'/\redextwo)) \setminus \names(\redseqthree'/(\tm'/\redextwo)) & \text{by \ih} \\
+    & = & (\names(\redex/\tm') \setminus \names(\redextwo/\tm')) \setminus \names(\redseqthree'/(\tm'/\redextwo)) & \text{by \rlem{cube_lemma_for_simulation_residuals}} \\
+    & = & \names(\redex/\tm') \setminus \names(\redseqthree/\tm') & \text{since $\redseqthree/\tm' = (\redextwo/\tm')(\redseqthree'/(\tm'/\redextwo))$}
+  \end{array}
+\]
 
